# P3e - Vacate grace window: P3e-natural
# @question: OPT-IN, runs for hours. Does a REAL backfill preemption look like condor_vacate_job (same signal, same grace)? Waits for a natural eviction.
# @sites: chtc_backfill
# @optin
# @triggers: 
# The probe logs the signal, ignores it, and keeps writing a 1 s heartbeat (streamed stdout,
# and a file on /staging where available) until HTCondor kills it. Last heartbeat - signal time = grace.
# It checkpoints once at step 5 (exit 85, in-place restart). After the eviction the job
# is rescheduled into a new sandbox; seeing that checkpoint come back, it exits 0 at once.
checkpoint_exit_code      = 85
transfer_checkpoint_files = ckpt
transfer_output_files     = ckpt, out
stream_output = true
stream_error  = true
periodic_remove = ((time() - QDate) > 8*3600) || (JobStatus == 5)
arguments = $(PROBE_ARGS) --on-sigterm ignore --heartbeat-every 1 --voluntary-exit-at 5 --exit-on-restart --total-steps 21600 $(HEARTBEAT_ARGS) 
